    "collection-faq": {
      "type": "collection-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "f1": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Closed Sole or Open Sole: what's the difference?",
            "answer": "<p>The grip is the same. The difference is feel. Closed Sole covers the whole bottom of your foot, heel included. Open Sole leaves the heel open, with a mid-foot vent for a barefoot feel. Toes stay free on both.</p><p><a href=\"/pages/compare-open-closed-sole\">See Closed vs Open side by side</a></p>"
          }
        },
        "f2": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Tired of grip socks that slip?",
            "answer": "<p>Grip socks slip. When your feet move, you can't fully commit, and your focus goes with them. Barreletics put one continuous grip into the sole, so you sink deeper and hold longer. Grip isn't optional.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f3": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Best alternative to Pilates socks, yoga socks & barre grip socks?",
            "answer": "<p>Barreletics. Grip socks rely on dots and fabric, and they slide. Our 360° grip system is one continuous grip built into the sole, so you can sink into footwork, water ski, and Super Lunge and stay there. Built for Pilates and barre. Closed Sole or Open Sole, same grip.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f4": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Which machines and disciplines are they built for?",
            "answer": "<p>Pilates and barre first: reformer, Cadillac reformer, Chair, Tower, Megaformer, Lagree, Classical Pilates, and mat. The same 360° grip system holds on the carriage, the platform, and the floor. Some people also love them for TRX and yoga on and off the mat. Many wear them to hot Pilates and hot yoga too, with a thin sock if they sweat a lot. Closed Sole and Open Sole grip the same.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f5": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Reformer, Cadillac, Chair & Tower: will they hold on Classical apparatus?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. On the reformer: footwork series (toes, arches, heels, tendon stretch), elephant, knee stretches, and the long stretch series demand continuous underfoot contact. On the Cadillac / trapeze table: push-through and parakeet need grip that holds the bar, not a sock that slides off mid-exercise. Bridging and footwork on the Chair or reformer stay locked without sock resets. Same grip system in Closed Sole or Open Sole.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f6": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Megaformer, Lagree & barre — named moves that punish grip socks?",
            "answer": "<p>Megaformer and Lagree: Super Lunge, Elevator Lunge, Catfish, Bear, and Plank to Pike load the foot laterally, and silicone dot socks slide. At the barre: flat back chair, water ski, relevé, plié, and seat-work pulses need feet that don't walk out of the hold. Same 360° grip system in every color above.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f7": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I wear them with or without socks?",
            "answer": "<p>They're made to be worn barefoot. Plenty of customers add a thin sock anyway: to keep their toes covered, to stay warm, or to handle sweat in a hot class. Your practice, your call.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f8": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Yoga flows — chair pose to downward dog?",
            "answer": "<p>Made for Pilates and barre first. Yoga is a bonus: chair pose, warrior, downward dog, and standing balances hold on or off the mat, toes free to splay. Great for TRX too. Closed Sole or Open Sole, same grip.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f9": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I clean them?",
            "answer": "<p>Hand wash with warm soapy water. They dry in seconds. That's it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f10": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I pick my size?",
            "answer": "<p>Go with your regular shoe size. They fit snug, like a second skin, and there's no break-in. A narrow or wide foot can shift your size, so check the <a href=\"/pages/performance-skins-size-chart\">size guide</a> before you order.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f11": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What's your return and warranty policy?",
            "answer": "<p>You have 30 days to return or exchange. Every pair also has a 90-day warranty against manufacturing defects. Full details on our <a href=\"/pages/returns\">returns page</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f12": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you ship across the US and internationally?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. We ship fast across the US and to 190+ countries worldwide.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
